  <issue>
  L010: SQLFluff 0.9.1 (and later) capitalize columns named year/month when used as the second parameters in PARSE_DATE
## Expected Behaviour
When run on a SQL file containing a line like PARSE_DATE("%Y", year), SQLFluff should realize that year must be a variable rather than an SQL keyword this context and not request that it is capitalized.

## Observed Behavior
For this function year and month is treated like SQL keywords rather than column names when used in the second argument.

## Steps to Reproduce
(1). Generate a SQL file of the form:
```sql
SELECT
    PARSE_DATE("%Y%m", CONCAT(year, month)) AS date
FROM
    model
```
(2). Set BigQuery as the dialect and run sqlfluff lint on this file.

Output is:
```
L:   1 | P:  34 | L010 | Keywords must be upper case.
L:   1 | P:  40 | L010 | Keywords must be upper case.
```


## Dialect
BigQuery

## Version
SQLFluff version is 0.9.3 (although this is not an issue in SQLFluff 0.9.0).  Python version is 3.8.1.0.
(I'm using DBT but the same issue occurs when not using dbt as a template).

## Configuration
```
[sqlfluff]
dialect = bigquery
exclude_rules = L003,L008,L011,L014,L016,L029,L031,L034

[sqlfluff:rules]
max_line_length = 120
comma_style = leading

[sqlfluff:rules:L010]
capitalisation_policy = upper

[sqlfluff:rules:L030]
capitalisation_policy = upper
```
  </issue>
  
